// Title: UAC Bypass With Fake DLL
// Sigma ID: a5ea83a7-05a5-44c1-be2e-addccbbd8c03
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: oscd.community, Dmitry Uchakin
// Date: 2020-10-06 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1548.002, T1574.001
// Description: Attempts to load dismcore.dll after dropping it
// False positives:
//   - Actions of a legitimate telnet client
// References:
//   - https://steemit.com/utopian-io/@ah101/uac-bypassing-utility
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_uac_bypass_via_dism.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dism.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\dismcore.dll") and (not(FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\Dism\\dismcore.dll"))
